  "tagline": "A city that runs its own theatre, amphitheater, gym, golf course and gas company, around a downtown that did not exist before 2013.",
  "summary": "Sugar Hill was a town of 2,500 in 1980 and has ten times that today. It had no centre until the city built one: City Hall in 2013, then the E Center, with the Eagle Theatre and a public gym, in 2018, and The Bowl amphitheater behind them. The city also runs a golf course and its own natural gas utility. It sits in north Gwinnett County between Suwanee and Buford, a few miles below Lake Lanier.",
  "locationNote": "39 mi northeast of downtown Atlanta",
